{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC5 measured against a baseline. The spec's gate was ALREADY red on main before this story, and the cause sits outside this story's three antipattern families.\n\nBoth runs are full 3-epoch, no case cap, local-mode gate session, on the dirty working tree.\n\n| Run | Cases | Distinct failing | coverage | epoch_pass | elapsed |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Baseline (`origin/main`, this story's 3 files reverted) | 33 | 6 | 1.0 | `[false,false,false]` | 2027.9s |\n| With this story | 39 | 5 | 1.0 | `[false,false,false]` | 2626.2s |\n\n**All 6 of this story's new cases passed in all 3 epochs** — `R-reexport-identity-only`, `FP-reexport-is-the-contract`, `R-importshape-all-literal`, `FP-importshape-generated-surface-census`, `R-gatererun-subprocess-verdict`, `FP-gatererun-fixture-tree`. The story's AC1-AC4 and AC6 deliverables are good.\n\nEvery failure in both runs is a PRE-EXISTING false-positive case from another antipattern family — LOC ceiling, Rule 5, deliberate tightening, pre-existing-gap, sleep. Per-epoch:\n\n```\nBASELINE  e0: 3 failing   e1: 4 failing   e2: 3 failing\nE508      e0: 4 failing   e1: 3 failing   e2: 3 failing\n```\n\nNo clean epoch in 6 measured. The failing SET shifts between runs, so this is intermittent over-firing, not a deterministic wrong guard: re-running the 7 implicated FP cases once each produced 0 findings on all 7.\n\n**Why the gate cannot pass as configured.** `_gating_results` passes an epoch only if EVERY applicable case passes (`eval.py`). The dataset now holds 20 no-fire cases. The measured per-case false-fire rate is roughly 3.3/20 = 0.17 per epoch, so P(clean epoch) = 0.83^20 = about 0.02, and the gate needs 2 clean epochs of 3. At this false-fire rate the bar is unreachable regardless of what this story adds — which is consistent with it having gone unnoticed, because bug 77b6 means CI has not actually scored this spec since the raze-vet-ditch safeguard landed.\n\nRebased onto current `origin/main` b7c6ed6c834 (32 commits; none touch this story's 3 files, and the only `src/rebar/llm/` change is `workflow/lint.py`), so updating does not resolve it. Work committed as 4d153d4cc27.\n\nAC5 is not being reinterpreted or waived. Driving the pre-existing false-fire rate down is the work that makes it pass, and that is calibration of antipattern families this story did not add. Filing it as its own ticket and blocking this story on it, so this story closes against a genuinely green spec."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793815459338716007,"uuid":"d8764445-69c1-44bd-8ed2-20ca915b8949"}